READ, pre-registered before these numbers existed:
  |B-A| > 0.24                -> layer 9's split has a measured consequence
  |B-A| <= 0.24 and |C-A| > 0.24 -> bounded below the bar; the probe HAS resolution, so this is a real null and b0-16 closes as a correlate
  |B-A| <= 0.24 and |C-A| <= 0.24 -> NO RESOLUTION: a 43% branch-gain change is invisible to domain_loss anywhere, so the null says nothing about layer 9
  B WORSE than A does NOT mean the split is harmless -- it means the trained value beats the median, which is a different claim.
